        "worked_solution": "First, recall the following:\n\n- ${J}_{2}(1)$ represents a $2\\times 2$ Jordan block with $1$'s on the leading diagonal.\n\n- ${J}_{1}(-1)$ represents a $1\\times 1$ Jordan block with $-1$'s on the leading diagonal,\n\nTherefore, our Jordan blocks are given by\n\n$$\n{J}_{2}(1)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{J}_{1}(-1)=[\\begin{aligned}-1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe composition of our Jordan blocks gives the following block diagonal matrix:\n\n$$\n{J}_{2}(1)\\,\u2295\\,{J}_{1}(-1)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
